{
	"_units": "Combined arms A1 (docs/combined_arms.md 2.3.1, 2.4.3): one row per projectile ArmourModel resolves against vehicle plates. Gun rounds live here; launcher rockets and missiles stay in data/warheads.json with the same keys, and Shells.shell(id) reads both. kind: apfsds, apds, ap, api, heat, tandem_heat, he, hedp, hei, amp, efp, thermobaric, canister. calibre_mm: the projectile's diameter (overmatch, ERA triggering). pen_ke: [[range_m, mm RHA at 0 deg], ...], linearly interpolated, held flat past the ends. pen_ce: a shaped charge's mm RHA (range doesn't matter to a jet). he_kg: TNT equivalent of the filling (HE punch-through 25 x he_kg^(1/3) mm against the plate's physical thickness, and blast). normalise_deg: how far a KE round turns toward the plate's normal. ricochet_deg: [never below, always above], linear between. overmatch: a calibre this many times the plate's physical thickness can't be turned (no ricochet, the angle capped at 45 deg). fuze: {kind: none, pd (sensitivity_mm), pd_delay (delay_ms), piezo (graze_deg), tandem (graze_deg), proximity (prox_m), airburst (offset_m); self_destruct_m; modes: {mode: another fuze}}. arming_m: a fuzed round hitting closer than this is a dud. module_dmg: damage (hp_kj units) to what is behind the plate on a full penetration. spall: {count, cone_deg} (used from phase A2). round_id: the data/rounds.json round Ballistics fires that this row is (a bullet's vehicle numbers). incendiary: API, fuel fire chance x2. A3 (ShellFlight): muzzle_mps and drag (quadratic, per metre: a = g - drag x v|v|, tuned so docs/combined_arms.md 2.7.5's times of flight and drops come out within 10%), mass_kg (its KE on a soft vehicle), frag_m and frag_wounds (an HE filling's fragments on people, as warheads.json's). Every number is Proposed, rounded from public figures.",
